internal/celt adapts the following from the reference implementation published
in RFC 6716:

  laplace.go  the Laplace entropy coder, from celt/laplace.c
  energy.go   the coarse energy probability model and prediction
              coefficients, from celt/quant_bands.c
  alloc.go    the static allocation, per-band cap and log-width tables,
              from celt/modes.c and celt/static_modes_float.h
  interp.go   the allocation interpolation and fine/shape split,
              from celt/rate.c
  spreading.go  the spreading rotation and collapse mask, from celt/vq.c,
              and the spreading decision distribution, from celt/celt.c
  transforms.go  the Haar and Hadamard reshaping, the bit-exact cosine and
              log-tangent, the split angle resolution and the noise
              generator, from celt/bands.c and celt/rate.h

  pulsecache.go  the pseudo-pulse scale, the fixed-point logarithm and the
              pulse cost cache, from celt/rate.c, celt/rate.h and celt/cwrs.c
  bands.go    the band splitting recursion, the split angle distributions,
              the stereo merge and the band loop, from celt/bands.c
  tf.go       the time-frequency resolution decoding and its selection
              table, from celt/celt.c

  internal/celt/testdata/gen_bitexact.c reproduces four of those functions
  from the same source, to generate the vectors they are checked against.

